IMPORT prelude

-- Wildlife Act 1965 (Singapore) -- what counts as wildlife (s 2), the approval-based prohibitions on feeding, releasing, killing,
-- trapping, taking, keeping, dangerous devices, sale, export and import (ss 5A to 5C, 7 to 9), defence of property (s 6), their
-- maximum penalties, the other offences' maxima (ss 10, 11A, 12, 12B, 12G, 12E, 21), composition (s 12K), arrest without warrant
-- (s 12), forfeiture of a conveyance (s 12C) and the time limit on a repatriation direction (s 12E(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/WA1965.txt. The revised edition
-- incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the deposit also shows Act 23 of 2023 (wef 18 December 2023) and Act 15 of 2026
-- (wef 1 July 2026), the latter amending the penalties in ss 5A(3) and 5C(3)(b)(ii).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the prohibitions an ordinary person or
-- business meets and the enforcement rules with decision content. Not encoded: the Director-General's appointment and delegation
-- (ss 4, 4A, 5), the content of s 10 directions, trap removal (s 10A), search, seizure and examination powers (ss 11A to 11C, 12A,
-- 12B beyond penalties), forfeiture under s 12D, expenses (s 12F), vicarious and officer liability (ss 12H to 12J), jurisdiction
-- (s 12L), informer rewards and fees (ss 13, 14), notices, evidence, protection from liability and service (ss 15 to 19A),
-- exemptions (s 20) and the rules (s 21) beyond their penalty cap. Which species are "protected" and which
-- offences are compoundable are left to subsidiary legislation, none of which was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wildlife Act 1965 -- offences`

§§ `2 -- wildlife`

-- s 2: "wildlife" means "an animal that belongs to a wildlife species, and includes the young or egg of the animal"; "wildlife
-- species" means "any species of animals of a wild nature, but excludes domestic dogs and cats, horses, cattle, sheep, goats,
-- domestic pigs and poultry". "animal" includes "any mammal, bird, reptile, amphibian, fish or invertebrate".
DECLARE Kind IS ONE OF
    `a domestic dog`
    `a domestic cat`
    `a horse`
    `cattle`
    `a sheep`
    `a goat`
    `a domestic pig`
    `poultry`
    `any other kind of animal`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind, `the species is of a wild nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is wildlife` IF
        `the species is of a wild nature`
    AND CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `any other kind of animal` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5A to 5C, 6 to 9 -- the approval prohibitions`

-- s 5A(1): "A person must not intentionally feed any wildlife in any place unless the person has the Director-General's written
-- approval to do so." s 5B(1): the same for "intentionally release". s 5C(1): "intentionally kill, trap, take or keep".
-- s 7(1): must not, "for the purpose of killing, trapping or taking any wildlife, set, place or prepare in any place any spring gun,
-- engine, pitfall, sharpened stake, snare trap or other device which is likely to endanger human life, or cause grievous hurt",
-- without approval. s 8(1): must not "offer for sale, sell or export any wildlife (whether alive or dead), or any part of a
-- wildlife" without approval. s 9(1): must not "import into Singapore any living wildlife" without approval.
-- In each section, subsection (2): a person who has the approval "must comply with the conditions of the approval".
-- Only ss 5A to 5C say "intentionally". Only s 9 is limited to living wildlife.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `feeding`
    `releasing`
    `killing, trapping or taking`
    `keeping`
    `setting a dangerous device`
    `selling or offering for sale`
    `exporting`
    `importing`

DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `activity` IS AN Activity
    `the animal is wildlife` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person acted intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wildlife is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Director-General's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breached a condition of the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the occupier or person in charge of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wildlife was found damaging crops or property on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wildlife is protected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the course of an animal-related business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prohibition requires intent` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `feeding` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `releasing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `killing, trapping or taking` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `keeping` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prohibition reaches the conduct` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the animal is wildlife`
    AND (   (NOT (`the prohibition requires intent` (`the conduct`'s `activity`)))
         OR `the conduct`'s `the person acted intentionally`)
    AND (   (NOT (`the conduct`'s `activity` EQUALS `importing`))
         OR `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is alive`)

-- s 6(1): "Nothing in this Act makes it unlawful for the occupier or person in charge of any land to kill, trap or take any wildlife
-- found damaging or destroying the crops or any other property on the land." (2): the onus of proving the damage "is upon the person
-- alleging the fact". s 6 names killing, trapping and taking -- not keeping, selling or setting a device.
-- INFERENCE: s 6 does not excuse a s 7 device, since s 7 prohibits setting the device rather than the killing.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `defence of property applies` IF
        `the conduct`'s `activity` EQUALS `killing, trapping or taking`
    AND `the conduct`'s `is the occupier or person in charge of the land`
    AND `the conduct`'s `the wildlife was found damaging crops or property on the land`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
        `the prohibition reaches the conduct` `the conduct`
    AND (NOT (`defence of property applies` `the conduct`))
    AND (   (NOT (`the conduct`'s `has the Director-General's written approval`))
         OR `the conduct`'s `breached a condition of the approval`)

§§ `5A(3), 5B(3), 5C(3), 7(3), 8(3), 9(3) -- maximum penalties`

-- s 5A(3) (as amended by Act 15 of 2026): (a) a fine not exceeding $10,000; (b) second or subsequent conviction, $20,000 or 12
-- months or both. s 5B(3): $5,000. s 5C(3): (a) protected wildlife, $50,000 or 2 years; (b)(i) otherwise, in the course of an
-- animal-related business, $20,000 or 12 months; (b)(ii)(A) any other case $10,000 or 6 months; (B) second or subsequent conviction
-- $20,000 or 12 months. s 7(3): $20,000 or 12 months. s 8(3): (a) protected wildlife, $50,000 or 2 years; (b) otherwise $10,000 or
-- 12 months. s 9(3): $10,000 or 12 months -- with no higher tier for protected wildlife.
-- Imprisonment is given in months; 0 means the provision allows a fine only.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`'s `activity`
    WHEN `feeding` THEN
        IF `the conduct`'s `is a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000
    WHEN `releasing` THEN 5000
    WHEN `setting a dangerous device` THEN 20000
    WHEN `selling or offering for sale` THEN
        IF `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is protected` THEN 50000 ELSE 10000
    WHEN `exporting` THEN
        IF `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is protected` THEN 50000 ELSE 10000
    WHEN `importing` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE `the section 5C maximum fine` `the conduct`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 5C maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is protected` THEN 50000
    ELSE
        IF     `the conduct`'s `in the course of an animal-related business`
            OR `the conduct`'s `is a second or subsequent conviction`
        THEN 20000
        ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`'s `activity`
    WHEN `feeding` THEN
        IF `the conduct`'s `is a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 12 ELSE 0
    WHEN `releasing` THEN 0
    WHEN `setting a dangerous device` THEN 12
    WHEN `selling or offering for sale` THEN
        IF `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is protected` THEN 24 ELSE 12
    WHEN `exporting` THEN
        IF `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is protected` THEN 24 ELSE 12
    WHEN `importing` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE `the section 5C maximum imprisonment` `the conduct`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 5C maximum imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the conduct`'s `the wildlife is protected` THEN 24
    ELSE
        IF     `the conduct`'s `in the course of an animal-related business`
            OR `the conduct`'s `is a second or subsequent conviction`
        THEN 12
        ELSE 6

§§ `10, 11A, 12, 12B, 12E, 12G, 21 -- other offences`

-- s 10(4): without reasonable excuse failing to comply with a Director-General's direction on development or works, $50,000 or 6
-- months. s 11A(5): not stopping a conveyance when required, $10,000 or 6 months. s 12(3): refusing name and residence, or giving a
-- false one, $10,000 or 6 months. s 12B(5): failing to comply with an information or production notice, $10,000 or 6 months;
-- s 12B(6): a false or misleading statement, $10,000 or 12 months. s 12E(4): failing to repatriate, $10,000 or 6 months. s 12G:
-- obstruction, $10,000 or 12 months. s 21(3)(b): rules may make a contravention punishable with up to $50,000 or 2 years.
DECLARE OtherOffence IS ONE OF
    `disobeying a development or works direction`
    `not stopping a conveyance`
    `refusing name and residence`
    `ignoring an information or production notice`
    `a false statement in answer to an information notice`
    `failing to repatriate wildlife`
    `obstruction`
    `contravening the rules`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN OtherOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disobeying a development or works direction` THEN 50000
    WHEN `contravening the rules` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN OtherOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a false statement in answer to an information notice` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstruction` THEN 12
    WHEN `contravening the rules` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 6

§§ `12K -- composition`

-- s 12K(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the following:
-- (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000." (2): on payment, no further
-- proceedings. Which offences are compoundable is prescribed by rules (s 21(3)(a)), not encoded.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `12 -- arrest without warrant`

-- s 12(1): an officer "may stop and arrest without warrant any person who within his or her view commits an offence under this
-- Act". (2): "Such person must not be arrested if the person satisfies the ... officer as to the person's name and residence in
-- Singapore and that the person does not intend to abscond."
GIVEN `committed an offence in the officer's view` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied the officer of name` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied the officer of residence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied the officer of no intent to abscond` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may arrest without warrant` IF
        `committed an offence in the officer's view`
    AND (NOT (    `satisfied the officer of name`
              AND `satisfied the officer of residence in Singapore`
              AND `satisfied the officer of no intent to abscond`))

§§ `12C -- forfeiture of a conveyance`

-- s 12C(1)(a): the court may order a seized conveyance forfeited if "the person is convicted of the offence and the conveyance is
-- proved to have been used in the commission of the offence". (2): not a conveyance "(a) of more than 200 tons net; or (b) ... an
-- aircraft or a train belonging to a person carrying on a regular passenger service to and from Singapore". (4): not if "its owner
-- establishes that the conveyance was unlawfully in the possession of another person without the owner's consent".
GIVEN `the person was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the conveyance was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `tonnage net` IS A NUMBER,
      `is a regular passenger service aircraft or train` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owner established unlawful possession without consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may forfeit the conveyance` IF
        `the person was convicted`
    AND `the conveyance was used in the offence`
    AND `tonnage net` AT MOST 200
    AND (NOT `is a regular passenger service aircraft or train`)
    AND (NOT `owner established unlawful possession without consent`)

§§ `12E(3) -- time limit on a repatriation direction`

-- s 12E(1)(a): the Director-General may direct the owner of a conveyance to repatriate forfeited wildlife imported in it in
-- contravention of the Act; (2) at the owner's own expense. (3): the owner need not comply "unless the direction is made within
-- (a) 12 months after the date on which the wildlife ... was imported ...; or (b) 6 months after the date on which proceedings for
-- the offence ... are concluded or the date on which the offence is compounded, whichever is the later."
-- INFERENCE: while proceedings are pending, the later of the two dates has not yet arrived, so the direction is in time. Where
-- no proceedings are pending and none were concluded or compounded, only limb (a) is available.
GIVEN `months since import` IS A NUMBER,
      `proceedings are pending` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proceedings concluded or offence compounded` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since conclusion or composition` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repatriation direction binds the owner` IF
        `months since import` AT MOST 12
    OR  `proceedings are pending`
    OR  (    `proceedings concluded or offence compounded`
         AND `months since conclusion or composition` AT MOST 6)
